<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/065R">Remark <span data-tag="065R">9.3.4.8</span>.</a> In the situation of Definition <a data-tag="065Q" href="/tag/065Q">9.3.4.7</a>, any functor from $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ to $\operatorname{\mathcal{S}}_{&lt; \lambda }$ can also be regarded as a functor from $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ to $\operatorname{\mathcal{S}}_{&lt; \lambda '}$, for any $\lambda ' \geq \lambda $. In this case, replacing $\lambda $ by $\lambda '$ does not change the $\infty $-category of elements $\int _{\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}} \mathscr {F}$. Consequently, the condition that $\mathscr {F}$ is $\kappa $-flat does not depend on $\lambda $. </p>
